    "question": {
      ":question/id": "93f51a7c-e331-5a3a-b941-3dda7e732cf2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $5?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $3$ rows and the matrix $C$ since it has only $4$ columns. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $B$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(B)=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\".",
