    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1debb7a8-ba8d-5bad-a0da-b8f89922083d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $4?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $3$  rows.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has only $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=3.$ As we can see, the matrix $E$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(E)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $E.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e4f0a9d6-f490-54be-a418-59a82fd626db",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "cb027b7c-b880-5f8a-8064-95b261498246",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "16357e1a-b5e2-5564-a45f-d67ab471e47e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b4664f78-29e9-5767-9520-27a34bc3c629",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8c250650-d8c7-5705-88b3-e2c6a44e7a5b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c11446ea-bf9b-5950-8b3f-2a0d3c71f47d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
